  "_comment": "Map for the game screen (2026-11-02). Positions are NOT typed in: geodata.py looks each place up on Wikidata by its search terms and only accepts a result whose label contains must_contain, that sits inside bbox, and that lies within max_m metres of the rough lat/lng estimate given here (the estimate is only an anchor for that check - it is never drawn). Places that can't be verified are left off the map, and the Map button only appears once enough places verify (geodata.VIABILITY_*). Layers: 'historic' is a georeferenced period street plan, used only if its tiles exist under static/ (build them with tools/georeference_scan.py); otherwise it opens on the unlabeled dark street map, with OpenTopoMap terrain as an option. Each layer carries a CSS 'filter' (desaturate/tint/darken) so the base map stays in the background behind the markers instead of competing with them - central Petrograd's rivers, canals and street plan are largely unchanged since 1917.",
